    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKDg5MWFiZTA5M2JlMTgxYjFhNzY2ZWZjYTU4NmYzM2ViOGE3Mjc0NTc",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mikekinney@Mikes-MacBook-Pro.local",
        "date": "2026-11-09T03:05:47Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mikekinney@Mikes-MacBook-Pro.local",
        "date": "2026-11-09T03:05:47Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(app): standalone Pause and Home entries in the operation list\n\nA Pause / Home / Optional-stop entry is its own entity kind\n(schema::ProgramEntry + OperationMeta position), not an Operation, so\nsetup::operation_order and every walk on it (post tool/freshness gate,\nrest ahead, program sim, setup sheet, tool list, verify) never see one.\nprogram_entry::sequence orders ops and entries for the list;\nposting folds each entry into the PARAM AfterOperation word of the\nposted op before it (the per-op #110 word, byte-identical), honouring\nSuppress and \"Skip pauses and homes\"; an entry before every posted op,\nor a stop and a home in one gap, refuse the post by name.\n\nCommands: AddProgramEntry, EditProgramEntry (action / suppressed);\nReorderOperation, DeleteEntity, CreateOperation's append and\nDeleteSetup's refusal count positions over the sequence. Project file:\nan `entry` entity kind with an `entry` payload, no version rung (older\nreaders refuse the unknown kind by name). UI: add rows in every\noperation-list menu, an entry row with its own menu, entries drag like\nops.\n\nFixes #155\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
